[task-01] An obligation is attributed to the requirement its quoted text comes from.
    -> obligation-attribution-by-quoted-text  [invariant/explicit]
       An obligation is attributed to the requirement whose quoted text it comes from.

[constraint-01] An obligation carries a quotation of the task text it derives from.
    -> obligation-carries-quotation  [functional/explicit]
       An obligation carries a quotation of the task text it derives from.

[constraint-02] An obligation's quotation is located within the span of the requirement
    the obligation is attributed to, not merely somewhere in the task file.
    -> quotation-within-requirement-span  [invariant/explicit]
       An obligation's quotation is located within the span of the requirement it is
       attributed to, not merely somewhere in the task file.

[constraint-03] A quotation is located without regard to where lines are broken, so the
    same sentence is found whether the text wraps or not.
    -> quotation-linebreak-insensitive  [functional/explicit]
       A quotation is located without regard to where lines are broken, so the same
       sentence is found whether the text wraps or not.

[constraint-04] An obligation whose quotation falls outside the span of the requirement
    it was attributed to is re-attributed to the requirement whose span contains the
    quotation, when that requirement also yielded obligations.
    -> reattribute-out-of-span-quotation  [functional/explicit]
       An obligation whose quotation falls outside the span of the requirement it was
       attributed to is re-attributed to the requirement whose span contains the
       quotation, when that requirement also yielded obligations.

[constraint-05] Re-attribution never leaves a requirement that yielded obligations
    holding none.
    -> reattribution-preserves-nonempty-yield  [invariant/explicit]
       Re-attribution never leaves a requirement that yielded obligations holding none.

[constraint-06] An obligation is never discarded for a quotation that cannot be placed;
    it stays where it was attributed.
    -> unplaceable-quotation-stays-attributed  [error_handling/explicit]
       An obligation is never discarded for a quotation that cannot be placed; it stays
       where it was attributed.

[constraint-07] Every disagreement between an obligation's quotation and the requirement
